{"title":"2003 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Which of the following numbers is the <i>largest</i>?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d05cacd1344b8d1bb954961ca6925f36971216f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 3.2571 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 3.\\overline{2571} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 3.2\\overline{571} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 3.25\\overline{71} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 3.257\\overline{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"595\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first four decimal places of all the numbers are the same, but all we have to do is compare the hundred thousandths places of the numbers:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e51fdfc9c44b06a7454d5ae28fb03215d1cd1c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.2571$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> does not repeat, so its hundred thousandths place is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/456a28c14a313c1bb8947c9ab2c2c8385708694b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.\\overline{2571}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> repeats and the pattern starts out with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so its hundred thousandths place is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/4/344192602207acdaf57915e1ffe338f592f8f8a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.2\\overline{571}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> repeats and the pattern starts out with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so its hundred thousandths place is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/3/cd352c65f008ef47aad1e576ef32c9abe67aedd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.25\\overline{71}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> repeats and the pattern starts out with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so its hundred thousandths place is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d089dc6b62b8bb43888c342231818b9ee78c6553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.257\\overline{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> repeats and the pattern starts out with a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so its hundred thousandths place is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Of the answer choices, the number with the largest hundred thousandths place is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/74376d74ed526f611e1fad9a432506d4ca278ffc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 3.25\\overline{71}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"99\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202347\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.029 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 55/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3018/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:32604:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202347 and revision id 251689. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}